 509+ 6CBF              // page-watermark   -- n
 510+ 6CBF              // how much a 8K page can be filled: the tail of every heap page, from
 511+ 6CBF              // $1EFF to $1FFF, is never allocated. The 257-byte margin (a) lets the
 512+ 6CBF              // header that CREATE has just written run past the watermark without
 513+ 6CBF              // crossing the page (the longest is about 36 bytes, ending below $1F24)
 514+ 6CBF              // and (b) absorbs stray writes to BASIC's UDG area, $FF58-$FFFF (offsets
 515+ 6CBF              // $1F58-$1FFF), made by code that believes it is still poking BASIC's
 516+ 6CBF              // RAM: while vForth runs, MMU7 holds whichever heap page was fitted
 517+ 6CBF              // last, so such a write lands in this margin, not on a heap entry.
 518+ 6CBF                              Constant_Def PAGE_WATERMARK,   "PAGE-WATERMARK", $1EFF
